From 7cc4197150bb3ff0e2226239988227c15342be90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:28:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] yuzu_cmd: --window-rect and --aux-rect for a fixed two-window
 layout

Add --window-rect x,y,w,h (main window) and --aux-rect x,y,w,h (aux
window) so one virtual display can hold both windows at known places,
e.g. --window-rect 0,0,1920,1080 --aux-rect 0,1080,1240,1080 on a
1920x2160 display.

With a rect the window is created SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS instead of
SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE (on Windows SDL gives a resizable window
WS_THICKFRAME | WS_MAXIMIZEBOX, which a capture host may stretch to
fill the display), and SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN so it does not flash at the
default position; it is then moved with SDL_SetWindowPosition, sized
with SDL_SetWindowSize and shown. The aux window also gets
SDL_WINDOW_NOT_FOCUSABLE (WS_EX_NOACTIVATE on Windows, shown with
SWP_NOACTIVATE), so a tap on it never takes focus from the game window.
Without the flags every SDL_CreateWindow call passes the same flags as
before.

The value parser is std-only (src/yuzu_cmd/window_rect.{h,cpp}) so it
can be tested without SDL or the emulator. It keeps x+w and y+h within
32767 (Win32's 16-bit window coordinates, and clear of SDL's
SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED/CENTERED encodings) and takes a minimum size:
--window-rect passes the 640x360 minimum client size eden-cli sets
afterwards, --aux-rect 1x1. A bad value prints its reason and eden-cli
exits with failure.

The aux window's creation log now reports its pixel size. The ledger
lists emu_window_sdl3_gl.cpp and emu_window_sdl3_null.cpp as upstream
hooks.

